{"id": "EUVD-2026-102478", "enisaUuid": "c189191b-111b-3e57-9ebd-0968f02cd09b", "description": "ValueCell through 0.1.20 contains an unauthenticated server-side request forgery vulnerability that allows remote attackers to direct backend requests by setting an unvalidated provider base_url. Attackers can set base_url via the provider config endpoint and trigger POST /api/v1/models/check to reach internal or metadata addresses, read error responses, and capture stored provider API keys.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T14:31:07", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/valuecell-model-provider-check-unauth-ssrf", "https://github.com/ValueCell-ai/valuecell/blob/v0.1.20/python/valuecell/server/api/routers/models.py#L216-L261", "https://github.com/ValueCell-ai/valuecell/blob/v0.1.20/python/valuecell/server/api/routers/models.py#L569", "https://github.com/ValueCell-ai/valuecell", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/valuecell-through-0.1.20-unauthenticated-ssrf-via-api-v1-models-check"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111320", "GHSA-8m63-6jcp-c2m9"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "89619546-5d09-38e6-ac86-c7ab86a2cbb2", "product": {"name": "ValueCell", "vendor": {"name": "ValueCell-ai"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.1.20"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "077740a0-cfa6-3dc4-936f-5ac0f51f1965", "vendor": {"name": "ValueCell-ai"}}], "isExploited": false}